      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, the best time to replace a roof is late spring through early fall, especially early fall. Moderate temperatures around 45\u00b0F to 85\u00b0F help asphalt shingles seal properly without becoming brittle or overly soft.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Seasonal Breakdown in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Early Fall (Best Overall): Mild temperatures and drier weather create ideal conditions for sealing before winter snow arrives. Because demand peaks in fall, book contractors early.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Late Spring: Mild daytime temperatures let shingles bond well and prepare your home ahead of summer storms, though spring rain can cause brief delays.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Summer: Long daylight hours and steady weather speed up work, but high heat can soften shingles and make them easier to scuff. Summer thunderstorms also bring hail.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Winter: Cold weather can keep shingles from sealing right away, and snow or ice creates hazards and delays. Winter replacements still happen for urgent leaks or storm damage, often with more scheduling flexibility.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              2,
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "For more details on timing and local installation factors, see Olympus Roofing and USA Superior . Most users on agree that late spring to early fall\u2014especially early fall\u2014offers the best balance of moderate temperatures, dry conditions, and daylight while avoiding extreme heat.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Olympus Roofing",
            "link": "https://olympusroofing.com/the-best-time-to-replace-a-roof-in-utah/"
          },
          {
            "text": "USA Superior",
            "link": "https://usasuperior.com/best-time-to-replace-roof/"
          },
          {
            "link": "https://www.quora.com/When-is-the-best-time-of-year-to-replace-a-house-roof"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          2,
          6
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Are you planning ahead for a routine replacement, or dealing with active leaks or storm damage? Sharing your roofing material (such as asphalt shingles or metal) can also help narrow down timing."
      }
